#!RuleTest
#test CDISC-CG0043 expect=violation domain=SUPPAE
#note "FU-6 (PLAN-merge-followups), pooled two-study package. The SUPPAE AESOSP record of study S2 points at AE record (USUBJID 001, AESEQ 1), which exists only in study S1 (AESMIE=Y); USUBJID is unique per study only (SDTMIG 4.2.3), so S2's subject 001 has no AE record AESEQ=1. Child key [STUDYID, USUBJID, IDVAR, IDVARVAL] -> no parent in S2 -> AE.AESMIE not supplied -> fires. Under the old key [USUBJID, IDVAR, IDVARVAL] the S1 record with AESMIE=Y was taken as the parent -> no violation (the cross-study false negative this key closes)."
#library standard=sdtmig version=3-4
#expectViolationCount 1
#expectViolationAt row=1 STUDYID=S2
dataset SUPPAE label="Supplemental Qualifiers for AE"
col STUDYID  type=Char
col RDOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID  type=Char
col IDVAR    type=Char
col IDVARVAL type=Char
col QNAM     type=Char
col QLABEL   type=Char
col QVAL     type=Char
---
S2 | AE | 001 | AESEQ | 1 | AESOSP | Other Medically Important SAE | Description text
---

dataset AE label="Adverse Events"
col STUDYID type=Char
col DOMAIN  type=Char
col USUBJID type=Char
col AESEQ   type=Num
col AETERM  type=Char
col AESMIE  type=Char
---
S1 | AE | 001 | 1 | HEADACHE | Y
S2 | AE | 001 | 2 | NAUSEA   | Y
---
